{
  "id": "st-pauls-church",
  "name": "St. Paul's Church Hill",
  "notes": [
    "THE FLOATING ISLAND IS THE DEFECT THIS PLATE EXISTS TO KILL. The shipping",
    "plate is a diamond of ground in a void, and its church is about 80 native px",
    "— shorter than the player. Here the summit is a BUILT TERRACE: a walled",
    "crest across the top of the frame, and beyond and BELOW that wall two hazed",
    "bands of the town's roofs going down the hill, then the strait, then the far",
    "shore. Four planes of receding stuff behind the wall is what makes a hilltop",
    "read as a hilltop instead of as an island.",
    "",
    "SCALE. Nave 96px to the eaves, 148px to the ridge (4.6 players — the",
    "benchmark asks for 140), bell tower 196px plus its cap and cross, which",
    "leaves the top of the frame. The church is placed right of centre on the",
    "third; the graveyard fills the left; the processional path runs from the",
    "steps at the bottom of the frame to the west door.",
    "",
    "THE GRAVEYARD carries the writing. Four headstone silhouettes (round-headed,",
    "shouldered, broken shaft, plain slab) in irregular rows, plus ledger slabs",
    "and a standing cross — EM TERRA ESTRANHA, in a strange land, which is what",
    "half of them actually say.",
    "",
    "CULTURE MARKERS: the Cross of the Order of Christ on the padrao, the bell in",
    "the belfry, the Portuguese ledger slabs recut with Dutch names."
  ],
